                    insight_open:           `Funnel opened: you ran the genuine open-innovation turnaround — inbound licensing to launch Tritón fast, the dormant periphery monetised, the anti-corrosion core defended, watertight IP terms, the contested spin-out secured, and an operating model with KPIs to sustain it. External-idea yield rose past the goal, time-to-market closed on the benchmark, and R&D ROI moved decisively above 1.0× without selling the edge.`,
                    insight_closed:         `Defaulted to closed: by finishing Tritón in-house and keeping the budget internal, you re-ran the exact model that lost the race. Inbound openness was a speed lever you declined to pull — so external-idea yield, time-to-market and ROI stayed capped, and AquaShield kept the first-mover share of the €22M segment.`,
                    insight_firesale:       `Core sold off: you out-licensed the anti-corrosion know-how customers buy Lumen for. It raised cash this year and armed a competitor for the next — in two years your licensee undercuts you with your own technology. Openness is a scalpel; you used it as a fire sale, and ROI and value capture were capped as a result.`,
                    insight_leak:           `Opened without terms: you licensed the enzyme in but left the term sheet blank — non-exclusive, no field-of-use carve-out. The spin-out can license the identical technology to AquaShield, so the speed you bought came with no protection. Value capture isn't in the decision to open; it's in the terms, which is why it was capped here.`,
                    insight_hoard:          `Dormant IP hoarded: you kept all 140 patents in-house, so the ~98 dormant ones kept earning exactly zero while AquaShield monetised theirs. The side of the funnel never opened — the easiest open-innovation win on the board was left untouched, and yield and realised value were capped.`,
                    insight_mixed:          `A partial opening: some of the open-innovation moves landed, but the inbound, outbound, IP-terms and operating-model decisions didn't fully reinforce each other — enough gaps for the board to doubt whether the funnel will stay open after this cycle.`,
                    insight_escalation:     `You lost the contested spin-out: AquaShield's exclusive bid closed while you deliberated or walked, slamming the inbound door and putting the medical-coatings segment beyond reach. Open-innovation windows are time-bound and partners are contested — a missed window is rarely re-opened.`,
                    insight_nomodel:        `No operating model to sustain it: without an inbound-scouting function, an out-licensing desk and KPIs the board can hold you to, the deals you struck this cycle revert to the closed model the moment the project ends — exactly how Lumen got here in the first place.`,
                    insight_triton_lost:    `Tritón arrives 14 months late: by declining the inbound enzyme licence you ceded the first-mover share of the €22M premium segment to AquaShield and spent €3.6M to fight for the remaining scraps. The licence would have launched you in 8 months for €2.8M.`,
                    insight_yield_low:      `External-idea yield stayed low: too little of Lumen's pipeline value came from outside the firm, so the front of the funnel never really opened. Open innovation only pays when external ideas actually flow into the pipeline, not just into the strategy deck.`,

                    hint_closed:            `You're running the closed model — Tritón is on the slow internal path and the budget never crossed the boundary. Pivot to inbound licensing and rebalance the budget before the cycle ends, or you'll lose the next race too.`,
                    hint_leak:              `You opened without terms — the enzyme can reach AquaShield. Lock exclusivity and a field-of-use carve-out into the licence; value capture lives in the term sheet, not the decision to license.`,
                    hint_core:              `You're out-licensing the core — the one capability customers buy Lumen for. Pull the anti-corrosion know-how back behind the line and liberate only the periphery, before your licensee becomes your competitor.`,
                    hint_escalation:        `AquaShield is buying the spin-out out from under you. Move today — a binding option or co-investment — or the inbound door and the medical segment are both gone.`,
                    hint_hoard:             `The 98 dormant patents are still earning zero. Open the side of the funnel — license ≥3 peripheral assets to non-competing adjacent players — and turn dead IP into the €4M/yr AquaShield already collects.`,
                    hint_exposure:          `Closed-model exposure is dangerously high — the funnel is still mostly welded shut. Open both ends on purpose and protect the terms before the board deadline closes the cycle.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — yield is up, time-to-market is closing on the benchmark and exposure is low. Land it: build the operating model and frame openness as a scalpel to hold it through the board.`,

